hey guys maximum McGee here and a few  weeks back at GDC I had the pleasure of  checking out an early beta version of  totem totem comes from the development  team press play who some of you out  there may recognize as the developers of  max the curse of brotherhood their new  game is also a 2d side-scrolling  platformer but with the added twist that  you control two characters  simultaneously the two characters are  linked at all times so when you say move  to the left they both move to the left  and when you press the jump button hey  they both jump the only other ability  you have is to make your two characters  swap places now while this may not sound  too taxing it's critical for solving the  game's many puzzles as you can see  characters can only pass through  barriers that match their color things  start out pretty simple but quickly ramp  up in complexity as the game makes you  swap places mid jump to avoid obstacles  the game has a cooperative mode as well  in this mode you still control two  characters but they're both the same  color so in this scene one player is  controlling both of the red characters  while the other player is controlling  both of the blues both players must then  work together to guide each other safely  through color specific hazards now in  both modes you probably notice a lot of  orb collecting like that one right there  totem doesn't pressure players with any  sort of time limit but if you want to  get the best score you'll need to  collect all the orbs and not get  yourself killed along the way as each  death will subtract from your final  score developer press play is aiming to  have totem out on xbox one and xbox 360  this fall
 

